        <h1>Due diligence checklist</h1>
        <p class="lede">Check items as you go. Use the button to open your browser’s print dialog and choose “Save as PDF.” You can also download the same list as plain text. Nothing is sent to a server.</p>
        <div class="actions no-print">
          <button class="btn" type="button" data-print>Print or save as PDF</button>
          <a class="btn secondary" href="checklist.txt" download>Download .txt</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Border and identity</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Lawyer has checked whether the coordinates fall inside the 50 km border strip.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Seller’s identity matches the registry, not only a messaging app.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> If I am abroad, the <span lang="es">poder</span> names one property, one purchase, and an end date.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Registry</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span lang="es">Partida registral</span> identified.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Fresh <span lang="es">certificado literal</span> read by my lawyer.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Fresh <span lang="es">certificado de gravámenes</span> read close to signing.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Mortgages, embargoes, and dispute annotations understood.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Building is on the title (<span lang="es">declaratoria de fábrica</span>), or I know that only the land is registered.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Who signs</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Marital property regime checked. Spouse signs if <span lang="es">sociedad conyugal</span> requires it.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> If the owner died, every heir in the <span lang="es">sucesión</span> is in the process.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Every co-owner signs, or has given proper authority.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Municipality and money owed</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Zoning and <span lang="es">parámetros urbanísticos</span> allow what I think I am buying.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Construction license and <span lang="es">conformidad de obra</span> checked if there is a building.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Unpaid <span lang="es">predial</span> and <span lang="es">arbitrios</span> identified and allocated in the deal.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>On the ground</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Physical lot compared with the <span lang="es">plano</span> and the registry description.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Visit at more than one time of day, and in the rainy season if rain changes access.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Noise sources noted: discoteca, roosters, church, mototaxis.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Neighbors asked about disputes, flooding, water, and who the seller is.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Surroundings noted: construction, dumps, spraying, rivers, market, clinic.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Cracks, humidity, roof, drainage, tank, pressure, wiring, termites in the jungle.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Engineer versus informal <span lang="es">autoconstrucción</span> noted. Engineer hired if the structure worries anyone.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Rural extras</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Not community land, or my lawyer has explained why this file is different.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Water rights or irrigation reviewed with ANA in mind.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Access is a right, not only a neighbor’s permission.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Possession-only paper is not being treated as title. Formalization, if any, is priced as slow and uncertain.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Payment</h2>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Price will be paid through the banking system if it is above the current bancarización threshold.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Alcabala exemption confirmed for this year, not copied from a blog.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Notary, registration, and legal fees estimated by the people who charge them.</label></li>
          <li><label><input type="checkbox"> A cross-border accountant has been asked about home-country reporting.</label></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="fine">This list is a memory aid from personal experience. It is not legal advice. Your lawyer may add items and may tell you some do not apply.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
